            <ArticleTitle>Infectious transient dental-related paresthesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three instances of paresthesia in the oral cavity were resolved by nonsurgical endodontic therapy. Resolution of the condition supports the theory that pressure caused by an expanding infection and the associated inflammatory response result in paresthesia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
